WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.070
A careful examination of the period from
1873 to 1896 provides useful insight

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:16.520
into our current era of political division
and social separation. After the Civil War,

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.720
America's economic expansion was halted by
the Long Depression — the longest contraction

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.560
in US history, coinciding with
a society in flux, as America

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.109
transitioned from an agricultural
republic to an industrialized nation.

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:34.410
Political parties at the presidential
level remained unchanged, but at the

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.879
Congressional level, politics became
increasingly destabilized as we still

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:43.739
fought over the Civil War. This is much
like today, with candidates litigating

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:47.400
issues that have been fought for the
past 40 years. Changes seen in the

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.400
parties over the past few decades will
not be short-lived. We are living in an

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.920
era of social upheavals, when citizens
are constructing new social orders

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.030
and our parties are shifting to address
these upheavals. The trend towards

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.860
populism within the GOP and leftism in
the Democratic Party are symptoms of

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.049
these changes and are unlikely to abate.
What do you think about the changes in

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:14.850
America's political parties? Let us know
in the comments. Also, let us know what

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:19.290
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.140
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

